    <briefdescription>
<para>Symbolic description of one row before it is materialised in the matrix: a <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_n_c_f4_1_1_pre_row_a2d18e40c2f133ed5062a8d829cc901b2_1a2d18e40c2f133ed5062a8d829cc901b2" kindref="member">left</ref> * (something) * <ref refid="struct_n_c_f4_1_1_pre_row_aa3d0d207279ce1f8ef1103f1b8cf1be4_1aa3d0d207279ce1f8ef1103f1b8cf1be4" kindref="member">right</ref></computeroutput> triple. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="struct_n_c_f4_1_1_pre_row_aa5366e834fe2a5915fcd68c0b548c629_1aa5366e834fe2a5915fcd68c0b548c629" kindref="member">preRowType</ref></computeroutput> decides what <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_n_c_f4_1_1_pre_row_a60b0bdb425c71265b5a6423fd1d912c0_1a60b0bdb425c71265b5a6423fd1d912c0" kindref="member">preRowIndex</ref></computeroutput> points at: <computeroutput><ref refid="class_n_c_f4_a51df58acce453ffcd976d4bdfb5e8d40_1a51df58acce453ffcd976d4bdfb5e8d40ab2af009459984d359f5e64f8a1d92655" kindref="member">ReducerPreRow</ref></computeroutput> indexes either <computeroutput><ref refid="class_n_c_f4_a04c30758d9d3b9b5b4cf58a01debac44_1a04c30758d9d3b9b5b4cf58a01debac44" kindref="member">mGroebner</ref></computeroutput> (<computeroutput>&gt;= 0</computeroutput>) or <computeroutput><ref refid="class_n_c_f4_a28a953b4678397c2b34ddc66d73eddfb_1a28a953b4678397c2b34ddc66d73eddfb" kindref="member">mInput</ref></computeroutput> (<computeroutput>&lt; 0</computeroutput>, decoded as <computeroutput>-<ref refid="struct_n_c_f4_1_1_pre_row_a60b0bdb425c71265b5a6423fd1d912c0_1a60b0bdb425c71265b5a6423fd1d912c0" kindref="member">preRowIndex</ref> - 1</computeroutput>); <computeroutput><ref refid="class_n_c_f4_a51df58acce453ffcd976d4bdfb5e8d40_1a51df58acce453ffcd976d4bdfb5e8d40a8c937e82dbbfc9c9651ff09f66ec7667" kindref="member">OverlapPreRow</ref></computeroutput> is a freshly added overlap whose polynomial lives in the current cohort&apos;s <computeroutput><ref refid="class_n_c_f4_a992b563e9f6c1d87f74682ad35b103ba_1a992b563e9f6c1d87f74682ad35b103ba" kindref="member">mRows</ref></computeroutput>; <computeroutput><ref refid="class_n_c_f4_a51df58acce453ffcd976d4bdfb5e8d40_1a51df58acce453ffcd976d4bdfb5e8d40ac2b6fa0097faaa61d3f3ee3cad49e150" kindref="member">PreviousReducerPreRow</ref></computeroutput> refers back into <computeroutput><ref refid="class_n_c_f4_a429e9c26374beab1442cdd04463fd9df_1a429e9c26374beab1442cdd04463fd9df" kindref="member">mPreviousRows</ref></computeroutput>. The <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word" kindref="compound">Word</ref></computeroutput>s <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_n_c_f4_1_1_pre_row_a2d18e40c2f133ed5062a8d829cc901b2_1a2d18e40c2f133ed5062a8d829cc901b2" kindref="member">left</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_n_c_f4_1_1_pre_row_aa3d0d207279ce1f8ef1103f1b8cf1be4_1aa3d0d207279ce1f8ef1103f1b8cf1be4" kindref="member">right</ref></computeroutput> are the leading monomial decomposition needed to materialise the row. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
